# Next.js Frontend Rules (Agent PLM)

These rules apply to `apps/web/nextjs` — a Next.js 15 App Router app with React 19, TypeScript (strict), Tailwind CSS v4, and a Quarkus REST backend.

## Stack & Paths

| Item | Convention |
|------|------------|
| App root | `apps/web/nextjs/` |
| Source | `src/` |
| Routes | `src/app/` (App Router only — no `pages/`) |
| Components | `src/components/` |
| API clients | `src/lib/{entity}.ts` |
| Path alias | `@/*` → `src/*` |
| Package manager | `pnpm` |
| API base URL | `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL ?? "http://localhost:8080"` |

## App Router Architecture

### Server vs client components

- **Default to Server Components.** Pages and layouts are Server Components unless they need browser-only APIs.
- Add `"use client"` only when the component uses: `useState`, `useEffect`, event handlers (`onClick`, `onChange`), browser APIs, or hooks like `useRouter` / `useParams`.
- Keep client boundaries small. Extract interactive pieces into client components; leave static shell, headings, and layout in Server Components.

```tsx
// Good: server page composes client list
export default function SeasonsPage() {
  return (
    <AppShell>
      <h1>Seasons</h1>
      <SeasonList />  {/* "use client" inside SeasonList */}
    </AppShell>
  );
}
```

### File conventions

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `layout.tsx` | Shared layout; export `metadata` for SEO |
| `page.tsx` | Route UI (required export: default component) |
| `loading.tsx` | Suspense fallback (add when fetch latency matters) |
| `error.tsx` | Route-level error boundary (add for critical flows) |
| `not-found.tsx` | Custom 404 for a segment |

- Use `generateMetadata` for dynamic titles when entity names are known server-side.
- Do not create `getServerSideProps`, `getStaticProps`, or API routes in `pages/` — this project uses App Router exclusively.

### Routing & navigation

- Use `next/link` `Link` for internal navigation. Use `<a>` only for external URLs or direct API links.
- Use `useRouter` from `next/navigation` (not `next/router`).
- Use `useParams<{ id: string }>()` for dynamic segments (`[id]`).
- After create/update, redirect with `router.push(\`/{entities}/${id}\`)`.

## API Client Layer (`src/lib/`)

Mirror the `seasons.ts` reference implementation for every entity.

### Structure per entity file

1. **Types** — `{Entity}`, `{Entity}Status` (if applicable), `{Entity}Input`
2. **Private `request<T>`** — shared fetch wrapper
3. **Exported CRUD helpers** — `list{Entities}()`, `get{Entity}(id)`, `create{Entity}(input)`, `update{Entity}(id, input)`, `archive{Entity}(id)`

### Fetch conventions

```ts
const apiUrl = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL ?? "http://localhost:8080";

async function request<T>(path: string, init?: RequestInit): Promise<T> {
  const response = await fetch(`${apiUrl}${path}`, {
    ...init,
    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json", ...(init?.headers ?? {}) },
    cache: "no-store",  // PLM data is dynamic; do not cache by default
  });
  if (response.status === 204) return undefined as T;
  const body = await response.json().catch(() => ({}));
  if (!response.ok) {
    const message = typeof body.error === "string" ? body.error : `Request failed (${response.status})`;
    throw new Error(message);
  }
  return body as T;
}
```

- Parse backend `{ error: string }` bodies on failure.
- Use `archive{Entity}` (DELETE) — never expose hard-delete in UI.
- Pass `version` from `initial` on update for optimistic locking.
- Keep all fetch logic in `src/lib/` — components call these helpers, not raw `fetch`.

## Component Patterns

### Page layout

Every entity page wraps content in `AppShell`:

```tsx
<AppShell>
  <p className="text-sm tracking-[0.2em] text-[var(--accent)] uppercase">Core PLM</p>
  <h1 className="mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">{title}</h1>
  {/* page content */}
</AppShell>
```

- List page: heading, description, "New {entity}" `Link`, `{Entity}List`.
- New page: heading + `{Entity}Form` with `create{Entity}` + redirect.
- Detail page: heading + `{Entity}Form` with `initial` + `update{Entity}`.
- Add nav links in `AppShell.tsx` when introducing a new entity.

### Forms (`{Entity}Form.tsx`)

- Client component with `"use client"`.
- Use native `<form action={handleSubmit}>` with `FormData` — no form libraries unless the user requests one.
- Props: `initial?: {Entity}`, `submitLabel: string`, `onSubmit: (input) => Promise<void>`.
- Track `pending` and `error` state locally.
- Use `defaultValue` (not `value`) for uncontrolled inputs.
- Disable submit button while `pending`; show "Saving…" label.
- Surface API errors in a styled alert (`border-red-500/40 bg-red-500/10`).

### Lists (`{Entity}List.tsx`)

- Client component; fetch in `useEffect` on mount.
- Handle three states: `loading`, `error`, empty, and data.
- Link primary identifier (usually `code`) to `/{entities}/${id}`.
- Use semantic `<table>` for tabular data.

### Error handling in components

```ts
.catch((caught: unknown) => {
  setError(caught instanceof Error ? caught.message : "Unable to load {entities}.");
});
```

Never swallow errors silently. Never use `any` for caught values.

## Styling (Tailwind CSS v4)

- Global tokens live in `src/app/globals.css` — use CSS variables, not hardcoded hex in components:
  - `var(--background)`, `var(--foreground)`, `var(--muted)`, `var(--accent)`
- Import Tailwind once in `globals.css`: `@import "tailwindcss";`
- Dark theme patterns:
  - Borders: `border-white/10`, `border-white/15`
  - Surfaces: `bg-transparent`, `rounded-md`, `rounded-lg`
  - Primary CTA: `bg-[var(--accent)] text-black`
  - Muted text: `text-[var(--muted)]`
- Responsive: use `sm:`, `md:` prefixes (`sm:grid-cols-2`, `sm:text-5xl`).
- Fonts: loaded in root `layout.tsx` via `next/font/google`; reference `var(--font-geist-sans)` in CSS.
- Do not add CSS-in-JS libraries, styled-components, or separate `.module.css` files unless explicitly requested.

## TypeScript

- `strict: true` — no implicit `any`, no non-null assertions unless unavoidable.
- Prefer `type` over `interface` for DTOs (matches existing code).
- Use string union types for backend enums (`"DRAFT" | "ACTIVE" | "CLOSED"`).
- Nullable API fields: `string | null`, not `string | undefined` on response types.
- Optional input fields: `field?: string` or `field?: string | null` as appropriate.
- Export types from `src/lib/` and import in components — do not duplicate type definitions.

## Data Fetching Strategy (Current Phase)

This project uses **client-side fetching** via `useEffect` + lib helpers. Follow this pattern until Server Components data fetching is adopted project-wide.

When adding Server Component fetching later:
- Use `async` page components with direct `await list{Entities}()` calls.
- Pass data as props to client components.
- Use `loading.tsx` for Suspense boundaries.
- Do not mix client `useEffect` fetch and server fetch for the same data on one page.

## Performance

- Import only what you need; avoid barrel files that re-export entire modules.
- Use `next/image` for remote images (with `remotePatterns` in `next.config.ts` when needed).
- Use `next/font` for Google/local fonts — never load fonts via `<link>` in components.
- Lazy-load heavy client components with `dynamic(() => import(...), { ssr: false })` only when justified.
- Do not prematurely memoize (`useMemo`, `useCallback`, `React.memo`).

## Environment & Config

- `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` for browser-accessible values only. Never expose secrets in client bundles.
- Copy `.env.example` when adding new env vars; document defaults.
- `next.config.ts` uses `output: "standalone"` for Docker — preserve this.
- Do not change `outputFileTracingRoot` without understanding monorepo Docker layout.

## Verification

After frontend changes, run:

```bash
cd apps/web/nextjs && pnpm exec tsc --noEmit
cd apps/web/nextjs && pnpm lint
```

For entity work, also smoke-test UI at `http://localhost:3000/{entities}`.

## Do Not

- Add `pages/` router, middleware, or auth unless explicitly requested.
- Install UI frameworks (shadcn, MUI, Chakra) unless the user asks.
- Hardcode `http://localhost:8080` in components — use the lib-layer `apiUrl` constant.
- Put business validation in the frontend — backend `{Entity}Rules` owns invariants.
- Create one-off `fetch` calls in components — extend `src/lib/`.
- Use `useEffect` for form submission — use form `action` handlers.
- Skip `version` on update forms — optimistic locking will break.
- Add tests, Storybook, or CI changes unless requested.

## New Entity Checklist

When adding a new PLM entity UI, also read the `create-plm-entity` skill. Minimum frontend deliverables:

```
src/lib/{entities}.ts
src/components/{Entity}Form.tsx
src/components/{Entity}List.tsx
src/app/{entities}/page.tsx
src/app/{entities}/new/page.tsx
src/app/{entities}/[id]/page.tsx
AppShell nav link
```

Copy Seasons (`seasons.ts`, `SeasonForm`, `SeasonList`, `app/seasons/**`) as the canonical reference.
